--------------------------------------------------–

PRIVACY_CONTROLS_ENABLED=true
COOKIE_CONSENT_ENABLED=true

ANALYTICS_ENABLED=false
MARKETING_TRACKING_ENABLED=false
ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=
GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_ID=

AUDIT_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=365
TEMP_FILE_RETENTION_HOURS=24

--------------------------------------------------–

19. OUTBOUND HTTP AND WEBHOOK SECURITY

--------------------------------------------------–

HTTP_CLIENT_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
EXTERNAL_API_MAX_RETRIES=2
EXTERNAL_API_RETRY_DELAY_MS=1000

WEBHOOK_SIGNATURE_REQUIRED=true
WEBHOOK_MAX_CLOCK_SKEW_SECONDS=300

--------------------------------------------------–

20. TEST ENVIRONMENT

--------------------------------------------------–

Use a separate disposable database and separate service credentials.

Never reuse production DATABASE_URL, TEST_DATABASE_URL or payment secrets.

TEST_DATABASE_URL=
TEST_REDIS_URL=

TEST_EMAIL_ENABLED=false
TEST_PAYMENTS_ENABLED=false
TEST_AI_ENABLED=false

ENABLE_DEBUG_ROUTES=false
ENABLE_TEST_ENDPOINTS=false

E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
E2E_STUDENT_EMAIL=
E2E_STUDENT_PASSWORD=
E2E_REGISTRATION_EMAIL=
E2E_REGISTRATION_PASSWORD=
E2E_VERIFICATION_URL=
E2E_PROTECTED_DOCUMENT_URL=

--------------------------------------------------–

21. FEATURE FLAGS AND DEPLOYMENT NOTES

--------------------------------------------------–

Keep feature flags consistent with the implemented routes and services.

Disabled flags must be enforced server-side, not just hidden in the UI.

Validate required settings at startup and fail safely on invalid production

configuration. Do not print secret values during validation.

